        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Hard rule 12 (CLAUDE.md)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Network bytes are recognized once, in Rust, before anything else sees them. No raw bytes cross the bridge into C++: only JSON that Rust rendered (ADR-019 amended ADR-012's typed structs). unsafe lives only in wire-bridge and wire-client-ffi, no panic may be reachable from a packet, and the fuzz targets codec_decode, validate, json_recognize and transport_ingest guard the parsers." tooltip="Sources: CLAUDE.md (Hard rules 12); .claude/rules/rust.md; docs/WIRE.md (Fuzzing); docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-019" id="p3-rule">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="p3-1">
            <mxGeometry x="20" y="1329" width="784" height="80" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Channels (wire-transport/src/channels.rs): the sender's reliable flag picks one&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;ch0 ReliableOrdered: every send marked reliable. SkyMP's server sent RELIABLE_ORDERED and its client RELIABLE; ordered is the stronger and only adds ordering (ADR-019).&lt;br&gt;ch1 ReliableUnordered: configured, but only the reserved M0 family maps to it by default (Hit, HostedActor, InventoryApply); no SkyMP sender picks it today.&lt;br&gt;ch2 Unreliable: sends marked unreliable: movement, animation, a client's ChangeValues, OnEquip on parity, Host; and the server's relays of movement, animation and graph variables.&lt;br&gt;Channel order is send priority per tick: session traffic first, movement last." tooltip="Source: skymp/skymp-wire/crates/wire-transport/src/channels.rs; wire-bridge/src/lib.rs (send); skymp/skymp5-client/src/services/services/sendInputsService.ts; skymp/skymp5-server/cpp/server_guest_lib/ActionListener.cpp (SendToNeighbours calls)" id="p3-chan">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="p3-1">
            <mxGeometry x="830" y="329" width="970" height="123" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="&lt;b&gt;Movement and position&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• UpdateMovement (2, 10): both; ch2; 256 B. The client's sample [R1], relayed only after MovementValidation and the movement budget&lt;br&gt;• Teleport (20, 28): s2c; ch0; 64 B. Move an actor [R0]&lt;br&gt;• Teleport2 (31, 39): s2c; ch0; 64 B. The server's correction, the snap-back [R0]" tooltip="Source: skymp/skymp-wire/crates/wire-schema/src/lib.rs (TABLE), skymp.rs; wire-transport/src/channels.rs; directions and rungs from each message's doc comment; reliability from the senders (skymp/skymp5-client/src/services/services, skymp/skymp5-server/cpp/server_guest_lib/ActionListener.cpp, MpActor.cpp)" id="p3-f0">
          <mxCell style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=3;spacingBottom=3;strokeWidth=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="p3-1">
            <mxGeometry x="830" y="470" width="314" height="194" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
